---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Dumbbell } from 'lucide-react';
import Heading from '@/components/Heading.astro';
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CHARGEnorthLogo from '@/assets/charge-north-logo.jpg';
import professionalPhoto from '@/assets/professional-pfp.jpg';
import roboticsPhoto from '@/assets/robotics-photo.jpg';

const pageTitle = 'About | Logan Peterson';
const pageDescription =
  'Learn more about Logan Peterson, his education, and his FRC journey.';
const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://loganpeterson.org');
const siteUrl = new URL('/', site).href;
const profilePageSchema = {
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  '@id': new URL('/about/#profile', site).href,
  url: new URL('/about/', site).href,
  name: pageTitle,
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    '@id': `${siteUrl}#logan-peterson`,
    name: 'Logan Peterson',
    description: pageDescription,
    image: new URL(professionalPhoto.src, site).href,
    sameAs: [
      'https://linkedin.loganpeterson.org',
      'https://github.loganpeterson.org',
      'https://github.com/sharkingstudios'
    ],
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  {pageTitle}
  {pageDescription}
  pageImage={professionalPhoto}
  structuredData={profilePageSchema}
>
  <section class="py-12 md:py-16">
    <div
      class="grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(18rem,0.7fr)]"
    >
      <div>
        <Heading
          title="About Me"
          description="A little more about the interests behind my projects."
          className="mb-6"
        />
        <div class="prose max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
          <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
            Hi, I'm Logan Peterson. I have recently graduated from North
            Gwinnett High School and served as the Electrical Lead in FRC team
            1771. I was also a part of CHARGEnorth, my high school's STEM
            program. I love to build robots, program, read, and create video
            games. I bring a unique blend of technical expertise and creative
            problem-solving to every project I undertake. My journey in the tech
            world has been driven by a relentless curiosity and a desire to make
            a positive impact through innovation.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
            My interest in engineering grew by turning ideas into projects I
            could actually build and use. From my early Mini FRC Robot and retro
            Bluetooth controller to Terralift, a warehouse automation robot, I
            have enjoyed working through the each process including CAD,
            electronics, programming, and testing. The problems that keep me
            curious are the ones where all of those pieces have to work
            together. I find that figuring out why something is not working is
            often as interesting as building it in the first place.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
            Outside of robotics, I enjoy creating video games and being part of
            creative technical communities. I have built games such as Horizon
            Driving and Soupocalypse, and I was the lead organizer for Daydream
            Atlanta, a Hack Club game jam at Georgia Tech. I also enjoy reading,
            and I like finding new projects that let me combine technical
            problem-solving with something creative.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-8 flex">
          <a
            href="/blog"
            class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'default', size: 'lg' })}
          >
            <Dumbbell className="mr-2 size-4" />
            View My Work
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        class="aspect-[4/5] mx-auto w-full max-w-md overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-muted shadow-lg"
      >
        <Image
          src={professionalPhoto}
          alt="Logan Peterson"
          densities={[1, 1.5, 2]}
          quality="high"
          class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          style="object-position: center 25%;"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-muted/20 py-12 md:py-16 dark:bg-background">
    <div>
      <Heading
        title="Education"
        titleTag="h2"
        description="CHARGEnorth, the project-based STEM program at North Gwinnett High School."
        className="flex flex-col items-center mb-8 text-center"
      />
      <Image
        src={CHARGEnorthLogo}
        alt="CHARGEnorth logo"
        densities={[1, 1.5, 2]}
        quality="high"
        class="mx-auto mb-10 block h-auto w-full max-w-xl object-contain dark:brightness-0 dark:invert"
      />
      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12">
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          At North Gwinnett High School, I was part of CHARGEnorth, a rigorous
          STEM-based program that provides a comprehensive learning experience
          by integrating humanities and engineering. Designed around
          project-based research and investigation, the program challenged us to
          delve deeply into the course material. It fostered a profound
          understanding of STEM fields while cultivating essential skills such
          as critical thinking, problem-solving, and collaboration. This
          innovative pathway enriched my academic journey and prepared me for
          future endeavors in STEM.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Beyond the core curriculum, CHARGEnorth at North Gwinnett provides
          opportunities that enrich the learning experience. The program gives
          students access to advanced technology and resources for hands-on
          projects and real-world applications. It also brings in industry
          professionals for guest lectures and workshops, offering valuable
          insight into the practical side of STEM fields. Through STEM-related
          competitions and events, CHARGEnorth fosters innovation and a spirit
          of healthy competition. Being part of the program was a transformative
          experience that helped shape me into a well-rounded student ready for
          future challenges.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

